# Screens: Options > VR. The game's Options screen has a VR button, it opens the plugin's settings screen on its tabs,
# and leaving by OK keeps the settings and writes the settings file. Then Headset layers in the desktop window, turned off
# and back on: the window says it shows the eye alone.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: nothing built. The simulated Index has no Menu button apps can use (README, Controls), so the
# ---- game menu is opened with the keyboard by the harness; this file tests the Options screens, not the opening.

log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
expect headset steady
headset no-menu.png
key Escape
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenMainMenu

# The game menu stands in the world: 2 m ahead of the head (Menu distance), level, at the height of the eyes, and it
# stays where it opened while the head turns (Rendering/WorldMenu.cs).
headset game-menu.png
expect headset new depth 1.5 2.6
expect headset new at 0 0 15
head 0 1.6 0 20 0
wait 1
headset game-menu-head-turned.png
expect headset new follows world
head 0 1.6 0
wait 1

# ---- Options, then the plugin's VR button ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

click Options
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenOptionsSpace
click VR
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type == VROptionsScreen
# The screen's tab control has five tabs: Display, Comfort, Controls, Hands, Interface (Gui/VROptionsTabs.cs).
read screen
expect result contains VROptionsTabs

# Leave on the last tab, as a player would look through them.
set VROptionsTabs 4
wait 1

# ---- OK keeps the settings and writes the file -------------------------------------------------------------------------

click OK
wait 1.5
expect log VR options: leaving, nothing changed within 5
expect log Settings saved to within 5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenOptionsSpace
expect no log VR options: no tab line
expect no log Exception

# Back out of Options and the game menu.
key Escape
wait 1
key Escape
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay

# ---- Headset layers in the desktop window off: logged, and put back ----------------------------------------------------

include vr-option.inc mirrorLayers false isChecked was_mirrorLayers
expect log '/Desktop window: the headset.s layers are not drawn/' within 5
expect no log Exception

cleanup
include vr-option.inc mirrorLayers {was_mirrorLayers} isChecked _
